  "text": "Our findings regarding the prevalence of motility disorders align with previous large-sample studies. In the multicenter randomized Tube vs. Trabeculectomy Study, new motility disturbances were observed in 5% of the 101 patients who received a Baerveldt glaucoma implant, whereas no motility issues were detected in the trabeculectomy group at 1-year follow-up (22). Similarly, Robbins et al. reported that among 732 patients treated with an Ahmed valve implant, 29 (4%) developed persistent strabismus beyond six months post-surgery (16)."
